                  <msItem>
                     <title>Theodulfus Aurel.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Add. 33186 fols. 18--20 are flyleaves of a
                        manuscript containing works of Hugh of St Victor that belonged to
                        Westminster Abbey in s. xvii and was burnt in 1694 (M. R. James, MSS of
                        Westminster Abbey, p. 43 n. 35).</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="11XX">s. xii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_89">Byland, Yorkshire.
                        Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin. </orgName><p>'Liber sancte Marie de
                        Bellalanda. In hoc uolumine continentur libelli magistri Hugonis canonici
                        sancti victoris' (followed by a list, beginning with the Didascalion and
                        Isagoge, fol. 20v). The remainder of the original book is missing (it
                        contained works by Hugh of Saint Victor, as confirmed by the Savile of Banke
                        catalogue, no. 35); it went to Westminster Abbey and was burnt there in
                        1694. The section is bound with books from St Mary's abbey,
                     York.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir John Savile (d. 1607).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Savile sale 1861, lot 60.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"> </provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir Thomas Phillipps, baronet (1792--1872),
                     MS 24354. Sold Sotheby's June 1898, lot 15.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">G. Dunn, sold 1914 (lot 731).</provenance>
               </history>
